"""Evaluative adjectives: words saying a thing is useful, valuable, important, appealing,
harmful or capable (helpful, beautiful, powerful, successful, important, effective, ...).

Works on the current token, lower-cased, leading space dropped:
- adjectives ending in -ful (useful, helpful, beautiful, powerful, ...) fire strongest;
- a named list of other evaluative adjectives fires at a medium level;
- manner adverbs built on such adjectives (carefully, successfully, fully) fire a bit more;
- "just", "only", "less", "most", "best", "able" and the Chinese particles 的 and 有 fire weakly;
- everything else is 0 (the component is slightly negative on many other words, not modelled).
Values are the least-squares fit on training text."""

READS = ()

